## Standardize Domain backend selection

Context: Domain → Information used the shared tab rail with a full-width card,
which made the tab surface differ from the canonical application treatment.
The Knowledge Graph backend was also presented as a compact dropdown that did
not explain the available storage choices. This change introduces accessible
backend cards and removes graph-only details from ontology-only domains.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html
   Replaced the visible backend dropdown with responsive native radio cards,
   applied the standard tab-content surface, used existing product brand
   assets, and identified graph-only sections for conditional visibility.
2. src/front/static/domain/css/domain-information.css
   Added token-based backend card layout, selected, focus, disabled, and
   responsive states, including the Bootstrap floated-legend layout fix.
3. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js
   Synchronized backend cards with the existing persistence value and hid the
   migration, Dual Knowledge Graph, and Triple-Store Gateway sections for No
   Backend.
4. src/front/templates/domain.html
   Loaded the focused Domain Information stylesheet.
5. tests/units/front/test_no_backend_ui.py
   Added contracts for accessible card markup, real brand assets, standard tab
   structure, responsive CSS, synchronization, and graphless visibility.
6. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-30-domain-backend-cards-design.md
   Documented the approved interface and conditional behaviour.
7. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-30-domain-backend-cards.md
   Recorded the test-first implementation and verification plan.

